## Beat-to-media map

Cover every editorial beat using stable IDs. For speech-led work, cover the approved dialogue or narration; for silent, musical, ambient, or performance-led work, use checked source/master time. `none`, reuse, and named `code:` visuals are valid entries. Specify progression and intended effect, not only objects.

One row per defined beat; a whole-scene duration or “Model 2” is not exact voiceover coverage. Request independent cutouts/parts/poses for independent motion. Whole-frame opaque images need an intentional complete-shot use, not a midground label. Ask the user for external assets/choices and wait before finalizing the refined plan.

